{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" describe dense indices with no holes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and keep their laws. A conformer reports them only while it has no holes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Algorithms use this refinement to number the live vertices and edges with arrays while holes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exist, instead of hashing every vertex and edge they meet. The bounds are upper bounds only."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Positions are never reused, so a bound counts every position ever handed out, and nothing in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the library allocates by it. Position-keyed state goes through a paged map"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_PositionNumbers"},{"type":"text","text":"), O(live elements + pages)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to "},{"code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s laws:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"containsVertex(atPosition: p)"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly for the positions of live vertices, all in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexPositionBound"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexPosition(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex(atPosition:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are inverses, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the live vertices in increasing position. Likewise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"containsEdge(atPosition:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly for the positions in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", all in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgePositionBound"},{"type":"text","text":", which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" lists in increasing order."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without holes, the bounds equal "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and positions are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_numberedRows(outward:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" numbers the live vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lists, for each number, the numbers of its successors (outward) or predecessors, with the edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions beside them, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" order."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph.swift#L24","fileName":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph.swift"},"roleHeading":"Protocol","title":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols023SparselyIndexedDirectedA0P","symbolKind":"protocol","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"}],"role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph\/edgePositionBound","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph\/vertexPositionBound"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph\/contai